# lane-3090 uncensored profile (owner 11-01: "okay please go ahead. also i need a button similar to
# our vllm lane on the desktop. so i have two buttons to either start the uncensored or the regular lane")
# Sourced AFTER .env by lane-3090-boot.sh, so every other knob stays identical to production.
# Weights: Mochgolf uncensored W4A16 (same layout/sizes as production, tensor-checked 11-01) +
# production's FP8 PLE table, hardlinked into one folder (no extra disk).
MODEL_DIR=/home/ai-host/models/qwen38-uncensored-lane3090
# First name is what responses report; the second keeps clients that ask for the stock name working.
SERVED_MODEL_NAME="Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Uncensored Qwen3.8-Flash-Next"
# Own durable-KV tier: cached prefixes from the other weights would be silently wrong here.
KV_TIER_DIR=/home/ai-host/models/kv-tier-uncensored-pp   # 11-04 PP layout; TP4 tier kept for rollback
LANE_LOG=/home/ai-host/lane-uncensored-serve.log
# Disk tier capacity is PER GPU (x4). 11-01: 100 GiB/rank filled the NVMe and killed the lane;
# 8 GiB/rank = 32 GiB total (~1.1M tokens). Changing it needs a wiped tier dir.
KV_TIER_JSON='{"kv_connector":"SimpleCPUOffloadConnector","kv_role":"kv_both","kv_connector_extra_config":{"kv_offload_backend":"disk","disk_path":"/kv_tier/lane3090","disk_capacity_bytes":8589934592,"disk_buffer_slots":16,"disk_num_slots":665,"persist":true}}'
